# No anonymous bind may ever modify the tree.
#
# Any self-referential allow ACI - userdn="ldap:///self", or a userattr rule
# such as ipatokenOwner#SELFDN / managedBy#USERDN - can be satisfied by a
# credential-less bind. That let an anonymous client create entries under
# cn=otp via the "Users can create self-managed tokens" ACI.
#
# There is no authmethod value that means "the client sent no credentials":
# the ACI keyword authmethod="none" means "do not check the authentication
# method" and always evaluates to true, so a deny that ORs in
# "(authmethod = "none")" would deny to everyone. The only ACI-expressible
# test for a credential-less bind is the empty DN: an anonymous simple bind
# and a SASL ANONYMOUS bind both bind with the empty DN, which does not match
# "ldap:///all", while any authenticated bind (password, GSSAPI, certificate)
# has a real DN and does. The rule therefore denies userdn != "ldap:///all",
# and the "absolute" keyword makes the deny final: when the rule matches,
# access is denied immediately without consulting the other rules, so this
# closes the whole class of "anonymous principal performs a write"
# escalations regardless of which allow ACI would otherwise grant it.
# Authenticated binds (GSSAPI, password simple, ACI-exempt Directory
# Manager) and reads are unaffected. (An RFC 4513
# unauthenticated simple bind that keeps a real DN cannot be distinguished
# from a genuine bind by any ACI clause; keep
# nsslapd-allow-unauthenticated-binds off.)
dn: $SUFFIX
add:aci: (targetattr = "*")(version 3.0; acl "Deny all modifications for anonymous binds"; deny absolute (add,delete,write) userdn != "ldap:///all";)

# The Dogtag PKI database (o=ipaca) is a separate backend with its own ACI set
# and must be protected the same way. addifexist applies this only on servers
# that actually host a CA (where o=ipaca exists); CA-less servers skip it.
dn: o=ipaca
addifexist:aci: (targetattr = "*")(version 3.0; acl "Deny all modifications for anonymous binds"; deny absolute (add,delete,write) userdn != "ldap:///all";)
